  "result": "Perfect! Voucher support is complete. All 194 tests pass.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **VOUCHER_EXISTS error** to src/errors.js for when trying to apply multiple vouchers\n2. **Updated invoiceTotals()** to include voucher calculation:\n   - Returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n   - Calculation: `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n   - Voucher is applied *after* VAT, reducing the final amount\n3. **applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })** function in src/invoices.js:\n   - Takes a fixed amount in cents off the invoice total\n   - Returns ok(newInvoice) with `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n   - Validates:\n     - Invoice must be 'draft' (NOT_DRAFT error)\n     - Only one voucher per invoice (VOUCHER_EXISTS error)\n     - Amount must be positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n   - Never mutates the input invoice\n4. **13 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Voucher amounts in invoiceTotals calculations\n   - Applying vouchers to draft invoices\n   - Error cases: NOT_DRAFT, VOUCHER_EXISTS, AMOUNT_INVALID (zero/negative/non-integer)\n   - Total correctly reduced by voucher amount\n   - Vouchers clamped at zero (never negative totals)\n   - Voucher preservation through addLine, removeLine, issueInvoice\n   - Voucher with line discounts and VAT combined\n\nVoucher amounts reduce the invoice total after all calculations, allowing for fixed-value discounts independent of line items or percentages.",
